# Real Anime Reviews — line-ending normalization
#
# Why this file exists:
# Without this, Windows tools save files with CRLF line endings while some
# editors (or git itself) sometimes save with LF. Git treats every line as
# "changed" when only the invisible end-of-line bytes differ, which produces
# huge phantom diffs (every line of every file flagged as modified).
#
# This file tells git: detect text files automatically and normalize their
# line endings to LF in the repo, then convert back to the platform's
# native convention on checkout. Result: clean diffs forever, no churn.

* text=auto

# Force certain files to always use LF regardless of platform (good practice
# for shell scripts, config files that may run in WSL/Linux contexts).
*.sh text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Force certain files to always use CRLF (Windows batch files need CRLF
# or they may misbehave when run from cmd.exe).
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Mark binary files explicitly so git never tries to do line-ending
# conversion on them (that would corrupt them).
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.docx binary
*.zip binary
